      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be easier indeed. I had look at the patch you point to for the implementation and that\u0027s what prompted me to object. The method is exposed on an immutable built object but the state is stored in the system server with no obvious relationship, and the impl of the method gets the service to tell it.\nA shape where I build an object that follows every convention for being an inert bag of immutable fields, and a method on that actually reaches into the system server, seems at the very least completely out of sync with usual patterns of usage. A normal pattern could be something like IpSecService#startMigration(IpSecTransform).",
